WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.672
Devices are attribute-driven too, but
only through their own attributes,

2
00:00:04.672 --> 00:00:07.600
the device rows of the
store table in the recap.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.780
Dynamic device groups read things like
ownership, trust type and enrollment profile,

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.063
and Autopilot devices carry
markers a rule can select.

5
00:00:16.063 --> 00:00:19.462
Filters read Intune's own
inventory at check-in.

6
00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:21.437
The highpoint is the red panel.

7
00:00:21.437 --> 00:00:25.695
Writing a device's extension attributes
needs the right Graph permission,

8
00:00:25.695 --> 00:00:28.648
and it depends on the call:
a signed-in administrator

9
00:00:28.648 --> 00:00:31.600
uses one permission, an
unattended service another.

10
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.150
Book 05's sample now
uses the signed-in one.

11
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.210
Then, the dangers of
dynamic device groups.
